Curated by Dr. Rasmus Lindholm.

# About the exhibition

The Brightwater Maritime Museum invites visitors to follow the spice, tea and cotton routes that linked the world between 1600 and 1850. *Tides of Trade* tells that story through original ship ledgers, navigation instruments and a full-size reconstruction of a cargo hold that visitors can step into.

> The centerpiece is the 1783 log of the brig *Hesper*, shown publicly for the first time.

# Visiting

The exhibition is fully step-free.

